  "hashAlgorithm": "blake2b-256",
  "body": {
    "summary": "We have determined that this Parameter Change governance action is constitutional.",
    "rationaleStatement": "Article II, Section 6.3 of the Cardano Constitution states \"\"Hard Fork Initiation\" and \"Parameter Update\" actions shall undergo sufficient technical review and scrutiny as mandated by the Guardrails to ensure that the governance action does not endanger the security, functionality, performance, or long-term sustainability of the Cardano Blockchain.\"\n\nThe governance action with ID “gov_action14dr5yg75pchr2sz42djtuflpvx5qnsek29qg7s7cft8lzrqt5vrqqtqntpk” and title “Reduce minPoolCost to 75 ada and increase Plutus Memory Limits (Part 2)”, as a Parameter Change governance action, has undergone appropriate technical review through the Intersect Parameter Committee and Technical Steering Committee. This includes an assessment of the security, functionality and performance impact of the proposed changes to minPoolCost, maxTxExecutionUnits and maxBlockExecutionUnits.\n\nThe governance action complies with the relevant guardrails, being MPC-01/02/03, MTEU-M-01/02/03/04, MBEU-M-01/02/03/04a and MEU-M-01. It also provides a Reversion Plan as required by Appendix I, Section 2.6.\n\nWe therefore find this governance action **Constitutional**.",
    "precedentDiscussion": "None",
    "counterargumentDiscussion": "None",
    "conclusion": "As a Parameter Change, this governance action has undergone sufficient technical review and complies with the relevant guardrails in the Cardano Constitution, so is deemed constitutional.",
    "internalVote": {
      "constitutional": 4,
      "unconstitutional": 0,
      "abstain": 2,
      "didNotVote": 1
    },
    "references": []
  },
